{"id":"5c25794e-be72-4523-ace1-ee70aa3c0188","object":"chat.completion","created":1784834897,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    core = case['core_distance']\\n    dist_list = case['distances']\\n    # map node to index\\n    idx = {node: i for i, node in enumerate(nodes)}\\n    edges = []\\n    for a, b, d in dist_list:\\n        if a == b:\\n            continue\\n        w = max(core[a], core[b], d)\\n        # canonicalize: smaller node first\\n        if a < b:\\n            edges.append((w, a, b))\\n        else:\\n            edges.append((w, b, a))\\n    # sort by weight, then by first node, then by second node\\n    edges.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1], x[2]))\\n    # union-find\\n    parent = list(range(n))\\n    rank = [0] * n\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\\n            parent[rx] = ry\\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n        else:\\n            parent[ry] = rx\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n    selected = []\\n    total = 0.0\\n    for w, a, b in edges:\\n        if union(idx[a], idx[b]):\\n            selected.append({'source': a, 'target': b, 'weight': w})\\n            total += w\\n            if len(selected) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n    else:\\n        raise ValueError('Input graph is disconnected: cannot form a spanning tree')\\n    return {'edges': selected, 'total_weight': total}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with a single key \"implementation\" whose value is a Python source code string defining `solve(case)`. The code should compute core distances (already given in case), mutual-reachability edge weights, build a deterministic MST using Kruskal with union-find, handling ties via sorting by mutual reachability, then by node IDs. Return object with selected edges and total weight. Must use only standard library, no randomness, no mutation of input. Must raise ValueError for disconnected (should not happen given fixture? but contract says reject disconnected). \n\nFrom fixture: case has nodes list, core_distance dict, distances list of [node1, node2, distance]. We need to compute mutual_reachability for each pair: max(core[node1], core[node2], distance). Then sort edges by (mutual_reachability, node1, node2) with node1 < node2 canonical. Then run Kruskal: union-find with path compression and union by rank. Add edges until n-1 edges selected. If after processing all edges selected less than n-1, raise ValueError (disconnected). Return dict with \"edges\" list of dicts {\"source\": node1, \"target\": node2, \"weight\": mutual_reachability} and \"total_weight\": sum of weights. Also maybe need to include? The objective says \"return selected edges plus total weight\". So that's it.\n\nEnsure deterministic: sorting by weight then by node IDs (string sort lexicographically). Union-find uses node index mapping (list of nodes). Use stable sort.\n\nImplementation details: parse nodes list, create index mapping. For each distance triplet, compute mutual, ensure source < target (canonicalize). Then sort edges. Then union-find.\n\nReturn JSON-serializable: so dict with lists, floats.\n\nEdge cases: distances may include duplicate pairs? Not given, but we handle. Also core_distance for all nodes present. Distances list length should be n*(n-1)/2? Not necessarily but we process all. If missing some pairs? We'll compute only given distances; but MST requires all pairs? Actually mutual reachability uses core distances and given distances; if some pair missing, can't compute. But input seems to provide all pairs. For robustness, maybe compute all pairs from given distances? But we only have given distances. The spec says \"for each pair compute mutual reachability\". So only for provided distances. But MST must connect all nodes; if not all pairs present, may be disconnected. We'll just use provided pairs. That's fine.\n\nReturn only JSON-serializable: use float.\n\nWe'll include _case_nonce? Not needed.\n\nRaise ValueError if disconnected.\n\nNow produce JSON string with escaped newlines, etc.\n\nLet's write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1656,"completion_tokens":1053,"total_tokens":2709,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":578},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":120},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}